  note: bind a function of the program's own that calls it: in a header beside this file, `static inline <C result> hero_SQUARE(<C type> x) { return SQUARE(x); }`, with the C types the macro's documentation gives where the placeholders stand; then name that header in an `extern` group and declare `hero_SQUARE` there like any function, and clang holds that declaration to your function (§ 13)
